=== Special structural feature: α₇ = perfect triangle packings ===
At n=21, kmax=7. The ONLY way to pack 7 odd cycles into 21 vertices is:
  (3,3,3,3,3,3,3) = seven triangles, total 21 vertices = ALL vertices covered.
No other partition of 21 into 7 odd integers ≥ 3 exists (minimum 7×3=21, exactly).
Therefore: α₇ = number of perfect partitions of C_21 into 7 directed triangles.
α₇ = 12,571,712.

By symmetry of C_21 (21 rotations, each giving same α₇):
  number of non-rotationally-equivalent perfect triangle partitions = 12,571,712 / 21 = 598,653.4 — not integer!
  This means perfect triangle decompositions are NOT uniformly distributed across rotations.
  (Or: some decompositions are fixed by the 21-cycle rotation, i.e., rotationally symmetric.)

=== α₆ = 6-packings ===
Type (3,3,3,3,3,3): 6 triangles, 18 vertices, 3 uncovered     — one type
Type (3,3,3,3,3,5): 5 triangles + 1 pentagon, 20 vertices, 1 uncovered — one type
(Other types like (3,3,5,5,...) would need ≥22 vertices, impossible at n=21)
α₆ = α₆^{(3⁶)} + α₆^{(3⁵·5)} = 1,454,221,328 (combined, not decomposed)

